# Child Sexual Abuse and Exploitation (CSAE) Policy

## Our Commitment

We are committed to protecting children and preventing any form of child sexual abuse and exploitation (CSAE) on our platform. We maintain a zero-tolerance policy toward content, behavior, or activities that involve or promote CSAE in any form.

---

## Prohibited Content and Activities

The following are strictly prohibited on our platform:

- Any sexual content involving minors, including images, videos, text, audio, or illustrations  
- Grooming behaviors or attempts to solicit minors for sexual purposes  
- Sharing, requesting, or distributing child sexual abuse material (CSAM)  
- Content that sexualizes minors in any way  
- Any facilitation, encouragement, or promotion of CSAE-related activities  

Users engaging in such behavior will face immediate action.

---

## Detection and Enforcement

We take the following measures to prevent and address CSAE:

- User reports are actively monitored and reviewed  
- Accounts involved in CSAE-related activity are immediately suspended or permanently banned  
- Content violating this policy is removed without notice  
- We cooperate fully with law enforcement agencies when required  

---

## Reporting CSAE

If you encounter content or behavior that may involve child sexual abuse or exploitation, please report it immediately through the app or by contacting us at:

**Email:** support@yourappdomain.com  

Reports are treated with urgency and confidentiality.

---

## Legal Compliance

We comply with all applicable local, national, and international laws related to child protection, including mandatory reporting requirements. Where legally required, we report confirmed CSAE cases to relevant authorities.

---

## User Responsibility

All users are responsible for ensuring that their activity on the platform complies with this policy. Failure to comply may result in account suspension, termination, and legal consequences.

---

## Policy Updates

This policy may be updated periodically to reflect changes in laws, regulations, or platform standards. Continued use of the app constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.

